    description: Some("Six Olympic events in order — dash, long jump, javelin, hurdles, hammer throw, high jump — each gated behind a qualifying time or distance you must beat before the next one opens. Running is a matter of waggling left and right as fast as you can, while jumps and throws are a held button that sets your angle and a release that commits it."),
